/*! \page page_codec AnCH codec library documentation
 *
 * \tableofcontents
 *
 * \section codec_intro_seq Introduction
 *
 * AnCH codec library associates content types ( \ref anch::codec::MediaType "MediaType" ) with serialization and
 * deserialization of C++ values. anch-rest uses codecs for requests and responses bodies ; they do not depend on
 * HTTP, so that other libraries (messaging) read and write their contents with the same codecs.
 *
 * \section codec_libs_sec Libraries
 *
 * anch-codec is built with anch-rest (since 0.3, codecs were part of anch-rest in 0.2). The core has no format
 * dependency ; each format is a plugin library built according to its option. Plugins with external dependencies
 * are skipped with a CMake status message when their dependencies are not found.
 *
 * | CMake target | Option | Content |
 * | :----------- | :----- | :------ |
 * | \c anch::codec | | concepts, \ref anch::codec::MediaType "MediaType" and negotiation, limits, \ref anch::codec::Side "Side", \ref anch::codec::Text "Text", \ref anch::codec::Codecs "Codecs", formats registry |
 * | \c anch::codec-json | \c ANCH_CODEC_JSON (needed by anch-rest) | \ref anch::codec::Json "Json" (anch-json) |
 * | \c anch::codec-csv | \c ANCH_CODEC_CSV (anch-csv) | \ref anch::codec::Csv "Csv" (lists of described objects) |
 * | \c anch::codec-protobuf | \c ANCH_CODEC_PROTOBUF (Protobuf) | \ref anch::codec::Protobuf "Protobuf", \ref anch::codec::ProtobufJson "ProtobufJson" |
 * | \c anch::codec-thrift | \c ANCH_CODEC_THRIFT (Thrift and Boost headers) | \ref anch::codec::ThriftBinary "ThriftBinary", \ref anch::codec::ThriftCompact "ThriftCompact", \ref anch::codec::ThriftJson "ThriftJson" |
 * | \c anch::codec-all | | \c codec/all.hpp : every plugin built and \c anch::codec::Available |
 *
 * \code{.cmake}
find_package(Anch REQUIRED)
target_link_libraries(my-app PRIVATE anch::codec-json)
\endcode
 * See \ref install_sec "installation".
 *
 * \section codec_codec_sec Codecs
 *
 * A codec is a type with static functions: \c mediaType() and \c serialize / \c deserialize , with one of their
 * forms (value and stream ; plus \ref anch::codec::Side "Side" ; plus content type and side), see
 * \ref anch::codec::Serializer "Serializer" and \ref anch::codec::Deserializer "Deserializer":
 * \snippet{trimleft} anch-codec/examples/codec.cpp codec
 *
 * \ref anch::codec::contentTypeOf "contentTypeOf", \ref anch::codec::serialize "serialize" and
 * \ref anch::codec::deserialize "deserialize" call the richest form a codec defines:
 * \snippet{trimleft} anch-codec/examples/codec.cpp serialize
 *
 * \section codec_format_sec Data formats
 *
 * A data format ( \ref anch::codec::DataFormat "DataFormat": \c anch::json::JsonFormat , \c anch::csv::CsvFormat ) serializes
 * values with options, without depending on anch-codec. \ref anch::codec::FormatCodec "FormatCodec" makes a codec of
 * it: media type, options of each side copied from the format default options and configured by the format
 * \ref anch::codec::FormatPolicy "FormatPolicy" (specialized by its plugin, which also translates errors into
 * \ref anch::codec::ContentTooLarge "ContentTooLarge"). \ref anch::codec::Json "Json" is
 * \c FormatCodec<anch::json::JsonFormat> and \ref anch::codec::Csv "Csv" \c FormatCodec<anch::csv::CsvFormat> ; a new text
 * format gets its codec without code of its own.
 *
 * \section codec_side_sec Trust policy
 *
 * \ref anch::codec::Side "Side" is the trust policy of the codec user: \c SERVER reads data it does not control
 * (checked and bounded) and trusts what it builds ; \c CLIENT checks what it sends and trusts what it reads.
 * anch-rest servers use \c SERVER and clients \c CLIENT ; a message consumer reads with \c SERVER and a producer
 * writes with \c CLIENT .
 * - \ref anch::codec::Json "Json" checks anch-json fields constraints on values read with \c SERVER and on values
 *   written with \c CLIENT , and has mapping options per side ( \ref anch::codec::FormatCodec::options "options" ,
 *   configured by \ref anch::codec::FormatPolicy<anch::json::JsonFormat> "its policy"):
 * \snippet{trimleft} anch-codec/examples/codec.cpp model
 * - codecs without limit of their own read contents with \ref anch::codec::readBody "readBody", bounded by
 *   \ref anch::codec::maxBodySize "maxBodySize" (2 MiB for \c SERVER by default): larger contents raise
 *   \ref anch::codec::ContentTooLarge "ContentTooLarge" ( \c 413 in anch-rest servers).
 *
 * \section codec_select_sec Codecs selection and formats
 *
 * \ref anch::codec::Codecs "Codecs" is a list of codecs resolved at compilation: it selects the codec of a content
 * type when reading, and negotiates the codec of accepted media ranges ( \c Accept , q-values) when writing:
 * \snippet{trimleft} anch-codec/examples/codec.cpp codecs
 *
 * \c codec/all.hpp (target \c anch::codec-all ) is generated with the plugins built: it includes their headers,
 * defines \c ANCH_CODEC_JSON_ENABLED , \c ANCH_CODEC_CSV_ENABLED , \c ANCH_CODEC_PROTOBUF_ENABLED and \c ANCH_CODEC_THRIFT_ENABLED , and declares
 * \c anch::codec::Available , the list of their codecs (Json, Csv, Protobuf, ProtobufJson, ThriftBinary,
 * ThriftCompact, ThriftJson, then Text). Types described by an external schema (Protobuf messages, Thrift structures) are not
 * described by \c anch::Mapping : Json does not handle them ( \c anch::json::Mappable ), so the list selects the codecs
 * of their format.
 * Each plugin registers its format when its library is loaded ( \ref anch::codec::formats "formats", for
 * introspection: accepted media types, startup logs, ...):
 * \snippet{trimleft} anch-codec/examples/codec.cpp available
 *
 * \section codec_schema_sec Protocol Buffers and Apache Thrift
 *
 * \c protoc messages are read and written by \ref anch::codec::Protobuf "Protobuf" ( \c application/x-protobuf )
 * and \ref anch::codec::ProtobufJson "ProtobufJson" ( \c application/json , Protobuf JSON mapping) codecs.
 * Structures generated by <tt>thrift --gen cpp</tt> are read and written by
 * \ref anch::codec::ThriftBinary "ThriftBinary" ( \c application/vnd.apache.thrift.binary ),
 * \ref anch::codec::ThriftCompact "ThriftCompact" ( \c .compact ) and \ref anch::codec::ThriftJson "ThriftJson"
 * ( \c .json ). Their RPC (Connect, gRPC-Web, gRPC, Thrift over HTTP) is in anch-rest (see \ref page_rest).

 */
